What is Set in Java?
Set is an interface in the Java Collection Framework that stores only unique elements. It does not allow duplicate values.
A Set is a collection that contains only unique elements. If you try to add a duplicate element, it will not be stored.
Why do we use Set?

We use Set when:

We want to store unique values only.
We want to remove duplicate elements automatically.
We need fast searching (especially with HashSet).
We do not need to access elements using an index.
import java.util.HashSet;

public class SetExample {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        HashSet<String> fruits = new HashSet<>();

        fruits.add("Apple");
        fruits.add("Orange");
        fruits.add("Apple");
        fruits.add("Mango");

        System.out.println(fruits);
    }
}

