Map Interface
Map is an interface in Java that stores elements in key-value pairs. It does not allow duplicate keys, but it allows duplicate values.
Why is Map used?

We use Map when:

 We want to store data as Key → Value pairs.
 We want to search data quickly using a key.
 Keys must be unique.
It is useful for storing records like Student ID → Student Name.
example
