Queue 

Queue is an interface in Java that stores elements in FIFO (First In, First Out) order. It is mainly used when elements need to be processed in the order they are inserted.
Why is Queue used?

We use Queue when:

 We want to process elements in FIFO order.
 We want to manage tasks one by one.
It is used in printing, ticket booking, messaging systems, etc.

Example

Imagine people standing in a ticket counter queue.

Ravi
Priya
Kumar
Ravi came first → Ravi gets the ticket first.
Priya came second → Priya gets the ticket second.
Kumar came last → Kumar gets the ticket last.

This is called FIFO (First In, First Out).
Queue Methods
Method	Description
add()	Adds an element.
offer()	Adds an element (returns false instead of throwing an exception if it fails).
remove()	Removes the first element.
poll()	Removes and returns the first element, or null if empty.
element()	Returns the first element without removing it.
peek()	Returns the first element without removing it, or null if empty.
size()	Returns the number of elements.
isEmpty()	Checks whether the queue is empty.
