priority queue
PriorityQueue is a class in Java that implements the Queue interface. It stores elements according to their priority (natural sorting order) instead of insertion order.
Why is PriorityQueue used?

We use PriorityQueue when:

We want elements to be processed based on priority.
We need automatic sorting.
 It is used in task scheduling, hospital emergency systems, CPU scheduling, etc.

PriorityQueue Methods
Method	Description
add()	Adds an element.
offer()	Adds an element.
remove()	Removes the highest-priority element.
poll()	Removes and returns the highest-priority            element.(remove sthe first element)
peek()	Returns the highest-priority element          without removing it.(give first element)
element()	Returns the first element without removing it.
size()	Returns the number of elements.
isEmpty()	Checks whether the queue is empty.
clear()	Removes all elements.
sample program
import java.util.PriorityQueue;

public class PriorityQueueExample {
    public static void main(String[] args) {

        PriorityQueue<Integer> pq = new PriorityQueue<>();

        pq.add(50);
